#: src/functions.md:3
msgid "System Information"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:5
msgid ""
"`arch()` — Instruction set architecture. Possible values are: `\"aarch64\"`, "
"`\"arm\"`, `\"asmjs\"`, `\"hexagon\"`, `\"mips\"`, `\"msp430\"`, "
"`\"powerpc\"`, `\"powerpc64\"`, `\"s390x\"`, `\"sparc\"`, `\"wasm32\"`, "
"`\"x86\"`, `\"x86_64\"`, and `\"xcore\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:9
msgid "`num_cpus()`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Number of logical CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:10
msgid ""
"`os()` — Operating system. Possible values are: `\"android\"`, `\"bitrig\"`, "
"`\"dragonfly\"`, `\"emscripten\"`, `\"freebsd\"`, `\"haiku\"`, `\"ios\"`, "
"`\"linux\"`, `\"macos\"`, `\"netbsd\"`, `\"openbsd\"`, `\"solaris\"`, and "
"`\"windows\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:13
msgid ""
"`os_family()` — Operating system family; possible values are: `\"unix\"` and "
"`\"windows\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:16 src/functions.md:220
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:18
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"system-info:\n"
"  @echo \"This is an {{arch()}} machine.\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:28
msgid ""
"The `os_family()` function can be used to create cross-platform `justfile`s "
"that work on various operating systems. For an example, see [cross-platform."
"just](https://github.com/casey/just/blob/master/examples/cross-platform."
"just) file."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:33
msgid "External Commands"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:35
msgid ""
"`shell(command, args...)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> returns the standard output of "
"shell script `command` with zero or more positional arguments `args`. The "
"shell used to interpret `command` is the same shell that is used to evaluate "
"recipe lines, and can be changed with `set shell := […]`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:40
msgid ""
"`command` is passed as the first argument, so if the command is `'echo $@'`, "
"the full command line, with the default shell command `sh -cu` and `args` "
"`'foo'` and `'bar'` will be:"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:48
msgid ""
"This is so that `$@` works as expected, and `$1` refers to the first "
"argument. `$@` does not include the first positional argument, which is "
"expected to be the name of the program being run."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:52
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# arguments can be variables or expressions\n"
"file := '/sys/class/power_supply/BAT0/status'\n"
"bat0stat := shell('cat $1', file)\n"
"\n"
"# commands can be variables or expressions\n"
"command := 'wc -l'\n"
"output := shell(command + ' \"$1\"', 'main.c')\n"
"\n"
"# arguments referenced by the shell command must be used\n"
"empty := shell('echo', 'foo')\n"
"full := shell('echo $1', 'foo')\n"
"error := shell('echo $1')\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:67
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# Using python as the shell. Since `python -c` sets `sys.argv[0]` to `'-"
"c'`,\n"
"# the first \"real\" positional argument will be `sys.argv[2]`.\n"
"set shell := [\"python3\", \"-c\"]\n"
"olleh := shell('import sys; print(sys.argv[2][::-1])', 'hello')\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:74
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:76
msgid ""
"`env(key)`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Retrieves the environment variable with name "
"`key`, aborting if it is not present."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:79
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"home_dir := env('HOME')\n"
"\n"
"test:\n"
"  echo \"{{home_dir}}\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:91
msgid ""
"`env(key, default)`<sup>1.15.0</sup> — Retrieves the environment variable "
"with name `key`, returning `default` if it is not present."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:93
msgid "`env_var(key)` — Deprecated alias for `env(key)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:94
msgid ""
"`env_var_or_default(key, default)` — Deprecated alias for `env(key, "
"default)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:96
msgid "Executables"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:98
msgid ""
"`require(name)`<sup>1.39.0</sup> — Search directories in the `PATH` "
"environment variable for the executable `name` and return its full path, or "
"halt with an error if no executable with `name` exists."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:102
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"bash := require(\"bash\")\n"
"\n"
"@test:\n"
"    echo \"bash: '{{bash}}'\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:114
msgid ""
"`which(name)`<sup>1.39.0</sup> — Search directories in the `PATH` "
"environment variable for the executable `name` and return its full path, or "
"the empty list if not found. Requires `set lists`<sup>1.53.0</sup>."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:118
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set unstable\n"
"set lists\n"
"\n"
"bosh := which(\"bosh\")\n"
"\n"
"@test:\n"
"    echo \"bosh: '{{bosh}}'\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:133
msgid "Invocation Information"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:135
msgid ""
"`is_dependency()` - Returns the string `true` if the current recipe is being "
"run as a dependency of another recipe, rather than being run directly, "
"otherwise returns the string `false`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:139
msgid ""
"`num_jobs()`<sup>1.56.0</sup> — The value of `--jobs` or the empty list, "
"`[]`, if it was not passed."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:142
msgid ""
"`recipe_name()`<sup>1.53.0</sup> - Returns the name of the current recipe."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:144
msgid "Invocation Directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:146
msgid ""
"`invocation_directory()` - Retrieves the absolute path to the current "
"directory when `just` was invoked, before `just` changed it (chdir’d) prior "
"to executing commands. On Windows, `invocation_directory()` uses `cygpath` "
"to convert the invocation directory to a Cygwin-compatible `/`\\-separated "
"path. Use `invocation_directory_native()` to return the verbatim invocation "
"directory on all platforms."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:153
msgid ""
"For example, to call `rustfmt` on files just under the “current "
"directory” (from the user/invoker’s perspective), use the following recipe:"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:161
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if your command needs to be run from the current directory, "
"you could use (e.g.):"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:169
msgid ""
"`invocation_directory_native()` - Retrieves the absolute path to the current "
"directory when `just` was invoked, before `just` changed it (chdir’d) prior "
"to executing commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:173
msgid "Justfile and Justfile Directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:175
msgid "`justfile()` - Retrieves the path of the current `justfile`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:177
msgid ""
"`justfile_directory()` - Retrieves the path of the parent directory of the "
"current `justfile`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:180
msgid ""
"For example, to run a command relative to the location of the current "
"`justfile`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:188
msgid "Source and Source Directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:190
msgid ""
"`source_file()`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Retrieves the path of the current source "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:192
msgid ""
"`source_directory()`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Retrieves the path of the parent "
"directory of the current source file."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:195
msgid ""
"`source_file()` and `source_directory()` behave the same as `justfile()` and "
"`justfile_directory()` in the root `justfile`, but will return the path and "
"directory, respectively, of the current `import` or `mod` source file when "
"called from within an import or submodule."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:200
msgid "Module and Module Directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:202
msgid "`module_file()` - Returns the path of the current module file."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:204
msgid ""
"`module_directory()` - Returns the path of the parent directory of the "
"current module file."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:207
msgid ""
"`module_path()` - Returns the `::`\\-separated path to the current module."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:209
msgid ""
"`module_file()` and `module_directory()` behave the same as `justfile()` and "
"`justfile_directory()` in the root `justfile`, but will return the path and "
"directory, respectively, of the current `mod` source file when called from "
"within a submodule."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:214
msgid "Just Process and Executable"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:216
msgid "`just_executable()` - Absolute path to the `just` executable."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:217
msgid "`just_pid()` - Process ID of the `just` executable."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:218
msgid "`just_version()`<sup>1.55.0</sup> - Version of the `just` executable."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:236
msgid "String Manipulation"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:238
msgid ""
"`append(suffix, s)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Append `suffix` to whitespace-"
"separated strings in `s`. `append('/src', 'foo bar baz')` → `'foo/src bar/"
"src baz/src'`"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:241
msgid ""
"`prepend(prefix, s)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Prepend `prefix` to whitespace-"
"separated strings in `s`. `prepend('src/', 'foo bar baz')` → `'src/foo src/"
"bar src/baz'`"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:244
msgid ""
"`encode_uri_component(s)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Percent-encode characters in "
"`s` except `[A-Za-z0-9_.!~*'()-]`, matching the behavior of the [JavaScript "
"`encodeURIComponent` function](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/"
"JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/encodeURIComponent)."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:247
msgid ""
"`quote(s)` - Replace all single quotes with `'\\''` and prepend and append "
"single quotes to `s`. This is sufficient to escape special characters for "
"many shells, including most Bourne shell descendants."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:250
msgid ""
"`replace(s, from, to)` - Replace all occurrences of `from` in `s` with `to`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:251
msgid ""
"`replace_regex(s, regex, replacement)` - Replace all occurrences of `regex` "
"in `s` with `replacement`. Regular expressions are provided by the [Rust "
"`regex` crate](https://docs.rs/regex/latest/regex/). See the [syntax "
"documentation](https://docs.rs/regex/latest/regex/#syntax) for usage "
"examples. Capture groups are supported. The `replacement` string uses "
"[Replacement string syntax](https://docs.rs/regex/latest/regex/struct.Regex."
"html#replacement-string-syntax)."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:257
msgid "`trim(s)` - Remove leading and trailing whitespace from `s`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:258
msgid "`trim_end(s)` - Remove trailing whitespace from `s`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:259
msgid ""
"`trim_end_match(s, substring)` - Remove suffix of `s` matching `substring`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:260
msgid ""
"`trim_end_matches(s, substring)` - Repeatedly remove suffixes of `s` "
"matching `substring`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:262
msgid "`trim_start(s)` - Remove leading whitespace from `s`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:263
msgid ""
"`trim_start_match(s, substring)` - Remove prefix of `s` matching `substring`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:264
msgid ""
"`trim_start_matches(s, substring)` - Repeatedly remove prefixes of `s` "
"matching `substring`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:267
msgid "Case Conversion"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:269
msgid ""
"`capitalize(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert first character of `s` to "
"uppercase and the rest to lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:271
msgid "`kebabcase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `kebab-case`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:272
msgid "`lowercamelcase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `lowerCamelCase`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:273
msgid "`lowercase(s)` - Convert `s` to lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:274
msgid ""
"`shoutykebabcase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `SHOUTY-KEBAB-CASE`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:275
msgid ""
"`shoutysnakecase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `SHOUTY_SNAKE_CASE`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:276
msgid "`snakecase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `snake_case`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:277
msgid "`titlecase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `Title Case`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:278
msgid "`uppercamelcase(s)`<sup>1.7.0</sup> - Convert `s` to `UpperCamelCase`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:279
msgid "`uppercase(s)` - Convert `s` to uppercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:281
msgid "Path Manipulation"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:283
msgid "Fallible"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:285
msgid ""
"`absolute_path(path)` - Absolute path to relative `path` in the working "
"directory. `absolute_path(\"./bar.txt\")` in directory `/foo` is `/foo/bar."
"txt`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:288
msgid ""
"`canonicalize(path)`<sup>1.24.0</sup> - Canonicalize `path` by resolving "
"symlinks and removing `.`, `..`, and extra `/`s where possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:290
msgid ""
"`extension(path)` - Extension of `path`. `extension(\"/foo/bar.txt\")` is "
"`txt`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:292
msgid ""
"`file_name(path)` - File name of `path` with any leading directory "
"components removed. `file_name(\"/foo/bar.txt\")` is `bar.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:294
msgid ""
"`file_stem(path)` - File name of `path` without extension. `file_stem(\"/foo/"
"bar.txt\")` is `bar`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:296
msgid ""
"`parent_directory(path)` - Parent directory of `path`. `parent_directory(\"/"
"foo/bar.txt\")` is `/foo`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:298
msgid ""
"`without_extension(path)` - `path` without extension. `without_extension(\"/"
"foo/bar.txt\")` is `/foo/bar`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:301
msgid ""
"These functions can fail, for example if a path does not have an extension, "
"which will halt execution."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:304
msgid "Infallible"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:306
msgid ""
"`clean(path)` - Simplify `path` by removing extra path separators, "
"intermediate `.` components, and `..` where possible. `clean(\"foo//bar\")` "
"is `foo/bar`, `clean(\"foo/..\")` is `.`, `clean(\"foo/./bar\")` is `foo/"
"bar`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:309
msgid ""
"`join(a, b…)` - _This function uses `/` on Unix and `\\` on Windows, which "
"can lead to unwanted behavior. The `/` operator, e.g., `a / b`, which always "
"uses `/`, should be considered as a replacement unless `\\`s are "
"specifically desired on Windows._ Join path `a` with path `b`. `join(\"foo/"
"bar\", \"baz\")` is `foo/bar/baz`. Accepts two or more arguments."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:315
msgid "Filesystem Access"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:317
msgid ""
"`path_exists(path)` - Returns the string `true` if the path points at an "
"existing entity and the string `false` otherwise. Traverses symbolic links, "
"and returns the string `false` if the path is inaccessible or points to a "
"broken symlink."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:321
msgid ""
"`read(path)`<sup>1.39.0</sup> - Returns the content of file at `path` as a "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:324
msgid "Assertions and Error Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:326
msgid ""
"`assert(CONDITION, EXPRESSION)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Error with message "
"`EXPRESSION` if `CONDITION` is false. `EXPRESSION` may be "
"omitted<sup>1.53.0</sup>,"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:329
msgid "`error(message)` - Abort execution and report error `message` to user."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:331
msgid "UUID and Hash Generation"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:333
msgid ""
"`blake3(string)`<sup>1.25.0</sup> - Return [BLAKE3](https://github.com/"
"BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3/) hash of `string` as hexadecimal string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:334
msgid ""
"`blake3_file(path)`<sup>1.25.0</sup> - Return [BLAKE3](https://github.com/"
"BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3/) hash of file at `path` as hexadecimal string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:336
msgid ""
"`sha256(string)` - Return the SHA-256 hash of `string` as hexadecimal string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:337
msgid ""
"`sha256_file(path)` - Return SHA-256 hash of file at `path` as hexadecimal "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:339
msgid "`uuid()` - Generate a random version 4 UUID."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:341
msgid "Random"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:343
msgid ""
"`choose(n, alphabet)`<sup>1.27.0</sup> - Generate a string of `n` randomly "
"selected characters from `alphabet`, which may not contain repeated "
"characters. For example, `choose('64', HEX)` will generate a random 64-"
"character lowercase hex string."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:348
msgid "Datetime"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:350
msgid "`datetime(format)`<sup>1.30.0</sup> - Return local time with `format`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:351
msgid ""
"`datetime_utc(format)`<sup>1.30.0</sup> - Return UTC time with `format`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:353
msgid ""
"The arguments to `datetime` and `datetime_utc` are `strftime`\\-style format "
"strings, see the [`chrono` library docs](https://docs.rs/chrono/latest/"
"chrono/format/strftime/index.html) for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:358
msgid "Semantic Versions"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:360
msgid ""
"`semver_matches(version, requirement)`<sup>1.16.0</sup> - Check whether a "
"[semantic `version`](https://semver.org), e.g., `\"0.1.0\"` matches a "
"`requirement`, e.g., `\">=0.1.0\"`, returning the string `\"true\"` if so "
"and the string `\"false\"` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:365
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:367
msgid ""
"`style(styles)`<sup>1.37.0</sup> - Return a terminal escape sequence "
"combining the named styles in `styles`."
msgstr ""

#: src/functions.md:370
msgid ""
"The styles supported by version 1.37.0 and later can be used to duplicate "
"`just`’s own styles:"
